---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import { icon } from '../lib/icons';

const updated = '2026-10-22';
const contact = 'privacy@atlesque.dev';
---

<Shell page="privacy" title="Privacy policy" description="How the atlesque tools handle your data, and how visit analytics work.">
  <header class="panel-header">
    <div class="title-block">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <span class="badge">
        <Fragment set:html={icon('history')} />
        Last updated <time datetime={updated}>22 October 2026</time>
      </span>
    </div>
  </header>

  <article class="prose">
    <p class="lead">
      This policy covers the tools listed on <a href="/">tools.atlesque.dev</a> and the websites they run on (subdomains of
      atlesque.dev and atlesque.com, semina.be and amongusdetective.com). It explains what data is processed when you use
      them and what you can do about it.
    </p>

    <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Atlesque Media VOF</strong> is the controller for the personal data described here. For any privacy question or
      request, email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Visit analytics (only with your consent)</h2>
    <p>
      When you first open a tool, it asks whether it may count your visit. Only if you choose <em>Allow</em> does the tool
      load <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/">Cloudflare Web Analytics</a>. If you choose <em>No thanks</em>,
      or your browser sends a Global Privacy Control signal, nothing is loaded.
    </p>
    <p>With your consent, Cloudflare records for each page view:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the page address and the page you came from (referrer);</li>
      <li>your browser, operating system and device type, taken from the user-agent;</li>
      <li>your country, derived from your IP address;</li>
      <li>how quickly the page loaded (performance timings and Core Web Vitals).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Cloudflare Web Analytics sets no cookies, stores nothing in your browser and, according to Cloudflare, does not
      fingerprint visitors or track them across websites. We only see aggregated statistics, such as visits per page and per
      country; we cannot see who you are. We use them to learn which tools are used and to fix slow pages.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR, and the consent rule for reading information from your device in the
      ePrivacy Directive as implemented in Belgian law). You can withdraw it at any time with the small shield button in the
      corner of each tool, or a <em>Privacy settings</em> link where a tool has one. Withdrawing does not affect visits counted
      before. Your choice applies to that one tool and is asked again after 12 months.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and security</h2>
    <p>
      All tools are delivered and protected by Cloudflare. To send you a page, Cloudflare necessarily processes technical data
      such as your IP address, the requested address and your browser's request headers, and may use them to block attacks
      and abuse. Legal basis: our legitimate interest in running secure, working websites (Article 6(1)(f) GDPR). We do not use
      this data to identify or profile visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Data stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>
      Many tools save your settings and work, such as theme, volume, progress or the text you entered, in your browser's local
      storage so it is still there next time. That data stays on your device and is not sent to us, unless a tool explicitly
      saves it online (see below). Your analytics choice is stored the same way, under the key <code>atlesque-consent</code>.
      These items are needed for the function you ask for, so they do not require consent. You can delete them at any time by
      clearing the site data in your browser.
    </p>

    <h2>Tools with accounts or online features</h2>
    <p>
      Some tools offer features that need a server: signing in with an emailed code, saving progress or groups online, or
      real-time sessions with others. For those, we process what is needed to provide the feature, such as your email address,
      the content you enter and the data needed to keep you signed in. Legal basis: providing the service you asked for
      (Article 6(1)(b) GDPR). We keep this data while you use the feature and delete it when you ask us to, unless a tool
      states a shorter period. Where a tool shows its own privacy notice, that notice adds to this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Who processes the data</h2>
    <p>
      We use <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> as our processor for hosting, content delivery, security, analytics and storage,
      under its Data Processing Addendum. Cloudflare may process data outside the European Economic Area, including in the
      United States; such transfers are covered by Cloudflare's certification under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework and
      by the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not sell your data, show ads, build profiles or make automated decisions about you.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access your data, to have it corrected or deleted, to restrict or object to its processing, to
      receive it in a portable format, and to withdraw consent at any time. Email <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>;
      we reply within one month. Because analytics are aggregated and contain no identifiers, we usually cannot link them to
      you.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also lodge a complaint with a data protection authority. In Belgium that is the
      <a href="https://www.dataprotectionauthority.be/">Gegevensbeschermingsautoriteit / Autorité de protection des données</a>;
      you can also contact the authority in the EU country where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We update this policy when the tools change how they handle data. The date at the top shows the latest version.
    </p>
  </article>
</Shell>
